 "evidence": "PlaSim's own temperature tendency of each process, zonal means at the row over the run's 3-day means; the correlated-k model follows the line-by-line model and runs on the same cloud-free 3-day mean columns, so it leaves out how the fluxes vary within the 3 days.",
 "reading_rule": "K/day of temperature at each GCM level, the ground first, and W/m2 through each level's mass; positive warms. diab is the physics' sum as the diabatic step hands it to the dynamics, and its difference from the processes' own sum checks them; sfc is the ground's sensible heat into the lowest layer, vdif turbulence, lsp large-scale condensation, conv Kuo convection, dca dry convective adjustment, nudge the top level's nudging. In a settled run the dynamics carries away the physics' sum.",
